{
  "info": {
    "name": "Mandate Storefront API",
    "description": "Phase 1 e-commerce API. Every route returns { ok: true, data } or { ok: false, error: { code, message } }.\n\nbaseUrl defaults to the live deployment. Switch it to http://localhost:3000 to test locally — both point at the same Supabase database.\n\nRun 'List products' FIRST: its test script captures product_id and single_stock_product_id into collection variables that later requests depend on. 'Create order' then captures order_id and razorpay_order_id.\n\nMoney is in paise everywhere. Rs 499 = 49900.\n\nFor the race-condition test you need a product with stock_count = 1. If none exists, run this in the Supabase SQL editor:\n  update products set stock_count = 1, status = 'available' where name ilike '%Shibori%';",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "https://mandate-theta-two.vercel.app"
    },
    {
      "key": "product_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "single_stock_product_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "order_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "razorpay_order_id",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "cron_secret",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Products",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List products",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('ok envelope', () => pm.expect(body.ok).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('returns products', () => pm.expect(body.data.products.length).to.be.above(0));",
                  "",
                  "// Capture ids for the rest of the collection.",
                  "const first = body.data.products[0];",
                  "if (first) pm.collectionVariables.set('product_id', first.id);",
                  "",
                  "const lastOne = body.data.products.find(p => p.stock_count === 1);",
                  "if (lastOne) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('single_stock_product_id', lastOne.id);",
                  "  console.log('stock_count = 1 item (use this for the race test):', lastOne.id, lastOne.name);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/products",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "products"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List products — filter by size",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/products?size=M",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "products"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "size",
                  "value": "M"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List products — filter by colour",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
